
  THE SPECTRAL BRIDGE: RATIONAL -> ALGEBRAIC -> TRANSCENDENTAL

======================================================================

  I. THE RATIONAL WORLD: THINGS THAT CAN BE COUNTED
  --------------------------------------------------

  Everything COMBINATORIAL is rational.

  Tiling chain eigenvalues (all rational, denominator 5):
    k= 0: lambda =      1 = +1.0000
    k= 1: lambda =    4/5 = +0.8000
    k= 2: lambda =    3/5 = +0.6000
    k= 3: lambda =    2/5 = +0.4000
    k= 4: lambda =    1/5 = +0.2000
    k= 5: lambda =      0 = +0.0000
    k= 6: lambda =   -1/5 = -0.2000
    k= 7: lambda =   -2/5 = -0.4000
    k= 8: lambda =   -3/5 = -0.6000
    k= 9: lambda =   -4/5 = -0.8000
    k=10: lambda =     -1 = -1.0000

  Spectral gap = 1/5 = 0.2000
  This is RATIONAL. Denominator = 5 = 5.
  At n=6: gap = 1/5. The golden prime controls the gap!

  Walsh coefficients (computed previously): all integer multiples of 1/2^10.
  hat_H(empty) = 29 (INTEGER). hat_H({(0,5)}) = -4 (INTEGER).
  Every Walsh coefficient is RATIONAL with denominator 1024 = 2^10.

  THE RATIONAL WORLD contains:
  - H values: {1, 3, 5, 9, 11, ..., 45} (all integers)
  - Walsh coefficients: Q (rational)
  - Eigenvalues: {0, +/-1/5, +/-2/5, +/-3/5, +/-4/5, +/-1} (Q)
  - Spectral gap: 1/5 (Q)
  - c3 counts, alpha values, score sequences (all Z)

  II. THE ALGEBRAIC WORLD: THINGS THAT CLASSIFY
  --------------------------------------------------

  The ISOMORPHISM CLASS flip chain lives in the algebraic world.

  The tiling explorer's trinity:
  - 12 SELF-DUAL classes (rational pole): T ~ T^op
  - 22 PAIRED classes = 11 conjugate pairs (algebraic pole): T != T^op
  - Total: 12 + 2*22 = 56 classes at n=6

  Self-dual classes have REAL eigenvalue contributions.
  Paired classes create CONJUGATE eigenvalue pairs,
  like sqrt(d) and -sqrt(d) for some rational d.
  These are ALGEBRAIC but (often) IRRATIONAL.

  The class-chain spectral gap is ALGEBRAIC:
  gap_class = 1 - |lambda_1|
  where lambda_1 is a root of a degree-56 polynomial over Q.
  So gap_class is algebraic irrational (generically).

  The golden ratio phi = 1.6180339887
  is ALGEBRAIC: root of x^2 - x - 1 = 0.
  It classifies the icosahedral world but is not rational.

  Algebraic irrationals in the project:
  sqrt(2) = 1.4142135624 (Leech lattice diagonal)
  sqrt(5) = 2.2360679775 (golden discriminant)
  2*cos(pi/7) = 1.8019377358 (octonion structure)
  phi = 1.6180339887 (golden ratio)

  THE ALGEBRAIC WORLD contains:
  - Class-chain eigenvalues (roots of integer polynomials)
  - Spectral gaps of isomorphism chains
  - The golden ratio phi (root of x^2-x-1)
  - Square roots of discriminants
  - Cyclotomic values (roots of unity)

  III. THE TRANSCENDENTAL WORLD: THINGS THAT EVOLVE
  --------------------------------------------------

  DYNAMICS are transcendental. The moment you ask 'how long?'
  or 'what temperature?' you leave the algebraic world.

  Mixing time (epsilon=0.01):
  t_mix = log(1/epsilon) / gap = log(100) / (1/5)
       = 4.6051701860 / 0.2
       = 23.0258509299
  This is TRANSCENDENTAL (log of rational = transcendental by Hermite-Lindemann).

  Partition function Z(beta=1) = 1.483052e+21
  Free energy F(1) = -ln(Z(1)) = -48.748389
  Both are TRANSCENDENTAL (sums of exp(integer)).

  Boltzmann entropy at beta=1: S = 4.379393
  Also TRANSCENDENTAL.

  Rapidity of the doubler:
  rho(2) = arctanh(1/3) = ln(2)/2 = 0.3465735903
  TRANSCENDENTAL (Hermite-Lindemann: ln(algebraic) is transcendental)

  Collatz drift = ln(3/4)/2 = -0.1438410362
  TRANSCENDENTAL (ln of rational).

  THE TRANSCENDENTAL WORLD contains:
  - Mixing times (log(algebraic)/algebraic)
  - Partition functions (sums of exp(integer))
  - Free energies (-log(transcendental))
  - Boltzmann entropies
  - Rapidity = ln(n)/2 (formal group logarithm)
  - Collatz drift = ln(3/4)/2
  - pi (hidden in modular forms, eigenvalue phases)

  IV. THE BRIDGE: HOW THE GAP CONNECTS THE THREE WORLDS
  --------------------------------------------------

  THE SPECTRAL GAP IS THE BRIDGE:

  RATIONAL side: gap = 2/m = 1/5 (at n=6)
  This number IS rational. It lives in the counting world.

  ALGEBRAIC step: The class-chain gap is algebraic irrational.
  Going from tilings to isomorphism classes introduces
  square roots (from paired class eigenvalues).
  The gap PASSES THROUGH the algebraic world.

  TRANSCENDENTAL side: Mixing time = log(1/epsilon) / gap
  The moment you ask HOW LONG to mix, you need logarithms.
  log(rational) = TRANSCENDENTAL (Hermite-Lindemann).
  The gap CROSSES INTO the transcendental world.

  The bridge at each n:
    n    gap (rational)     log(gap) (transcendental)       t_mix
    3                 2                  0.6931471806         inf
    4               2/3                 -0.4054651081       11.36
    5               1/3                 -1.0986122887        4.19
    6               1/5                 -1.6094379124        2.86
    7              2/15                 -2.0149030205        2.29
    8              2/21                 -2.3513752572        1.96
    9              1/14                 -2.6390573296        1.75
   10              1/18                 -2.8903717579        1.59
   11              2/45                 -3.1135153092        1.48
   12              2/55                 -3.3141860047        1.39

  V. THE THREE POLES AND THEIR NUMBER TYPES
  --------------------------------------------------

  The tiling explorer's trinity maps EXACTLY to number types:

  SELF-DUAL CLASSES (12 at n=6) = RATIONAL POLE
    T ~ T^op. Fixed under transpose.
    Their eigenvalue contributions are REAL RATIONAL.
    They are the 'integers' of tournament space.
    The H values of self-dual tournaments are
    fully determined by the CLASS (no pairing ambiguity).

  PAIRED CLASSES (22 at n=6) = ALGEBRAIC POLE
    T != T^op but T^op ~ T' for some other class.
    They come in CONJUGATE PAIRS, like sqrt(5) and -sqrt(5).
    Their eigenvalue contributions involve SQUARE ROOTS
    of rational discriminants.
    They are the 'algebraic irrationals' of tournament space.

  FLIP GRAPH PATHS = TRANSCENDENTAL CONTINUUM
    The continuous paths between classes in flip space.
    Evolution along these paths involves EXPONENTIAL DECAY:
    P(class_j at time t | class_i at time 0) = sum_k c_k * lambda_k^t
    For irrational t: lambda_k^t = exp(t * ln(lambda_k))
    = transcendental (exp of transcendental).
    The flip graph dynamics live in the TRANSCENDENTAL world.

  VI. THE HERMITE-LINDEMANN THEOREM AND TOURNAMENT DYNAMICS
  --------------------------------------------------

  Hermite-Lindemann (1882): If alpha is a nonzero algebraic number,
  then e^alpha is transcendental.

  Consequence for tournaments:
  1. Eigenvalues lambda_k are algebraic (roots of char. poly).
  2. The time evolution lambda_k^t = exp(t * ln(lambda_k)).
  3. ln(lambda_k) is transcendental (by Hermite-Lindemann,
     since lambda_k is algebraic and nonzero).
  4. For INTEGER time t: lambda_k^t is algebraic (power of algebraic).
  5. For REAL time t: lambda_k^t is transcendental (exp of transcendental).

  So INTEGER-TIME dynamics stay algebraic,
  but CONTINUOUS-TIME dynamics are transcendental.
  The discrete flip chain (integer steps) lives in the algebraic world.
  The continuous-time Markov chain lives in the transcendental world.

  Concrete example: eigenvalue 4/5 at degree 1
  lambda = 4/5 (RATIONAL)
  ln(lambda) = ln(4/5) = -0.2231435513 (TRANSCENDENTAL)
  lambda^1 = 0.8000000000 (RATIONAL)
  lambda^2 = 0.6400000000 (RATIONAL)
  lambda^pi = 0.4960759984 (TRANSCENDENTAL)
  lambda^phi = 0.6969414669 (TRANSCENDENTAL)

  At integer time: rational^integer = RATIONAL (stays in Q)
  At golden time: rational^phi = TRANSCENDENTAL (escapes to T)
  The golden ratio phi bridges algebraic -> transcendental!

  VII. THE RAPIDITY AS THE FORMAL GROUP LOGARITHM
  --------------------------------------------------

  The Cayley formal group F(x,y) = (x+y)/(1+xy) has:
  log_F = arctanh (the formal logarithm)
  exp_F = tanh (the formal exponential)

  The logarithm MAPS:
  RATIONAL inputs -> TRANSCENDENTAL outputs:
    n=2: x = 1/3 (RATIONAL) -> rho = 0.3465735903 (TRANSCENDENTAL)
    n=3: x = 1/2 (RATIONAL) -> rho = 0.5493061443 (TRANSCENDENTAL)
    n=5: x = 2/3 (RATIONAL) -> rho = 0.8047189562 (TRANSCENDENTAL)
    n=7: x = 3/4 (RATIONAL) -> rho = 0.9729550745 (TRANSCENDENTAL)
    n=42: x = 41/43 (RATIONAL) -> rho = 1.8688348091 (TRANSCENDENTAL)

  The formal logarithm IS the bridge from rational to transcendental.
  arctanh(rational) = transcendental (always, for nonzero input).
  This is why RAPIDITY lives in the transcendental world
  even though TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE lives in the rational world.

  VIII. SYNTHESIS: THE NUMBER TYPE HIERARCHY
  --------------------------------------------------

  STATICS (what IS)              -> RATIONAL / ALGEBRAIC
    H values, cycle counts, Walsh coefficients
    Eigenvalues, spectral gaps, characteristic polynomials

  DYNAMICS (what HAPPENS)         -> TRANSCENDENTAL
    Mixing times, evolution, partition functions
    Rapidity, free energy, entropy

  THE GAP bridges them:
    gap = 2/m (RATIONAL)
    gap^t for integer t (ALGEBRAIC)
    log(gap) = mixing rate (TRANSCENDENTAL)

  The three number types are NOT just mathematical abstractions.
  They are three LAYERS OF REALITY:
    Q (rational)       = what you can COUNT
    Q-bar (algebraic)  = what you can CLASSIFY
    R (transcendental) = what you can EXPERIENCE (time, evolution)

  Every tournament lives in Q (it's a finite combinatorial object).
  Every classification lives in Q-bar (eigenvalues of symmetry groups).
  Every process lives in R (mixing, relaxation, diffusion).

  The spectral gap is the EXACT POINT where counting (Q)
  meets classification (Q-bar) meets evolution (R).
  It is rational as a NUMBER, algebraic as a CLASSIFIER,
  and transcendental as a TIMER.

  Or more simply:
  THE GAP IS A RATIONAL NUMBER
  WHOSE LOGARITHM IS TRANSCENDENTAL
  AND WHOSE CLASSIFICATION ROLE IS ALGEBRAIC.

  One number. Three worlds. The bridge between them.

